# PUP Compose New Music for Sample Pack Benefitting Kids in Toronto

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from Pitchfork Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Newsletter Search Search News Reviews Best New Music Features Lists Columns Video Open Navigation Menu Menu Search Search News PUP Compose New Music for Sample Pack Benefitting Kids in Toronto Students from Community Music Schools of Toronto performed the eight new compositions By Jazz Monroe November 26, 2026 Photo by Getty Images Comment Loader Save Story Save this story Comment Loader Save Story Save this story PUP have donated a sample pack—comprising eight new compositions and their stems—to a music library in their Toronto hometown. The band’s Parkscapes Volume 5 is performed by students at Community Music Schools of Toronto, the charity that will receive proceeds from its sales. The pack will be available from December 11 at parkscapes.ca , priced at $19.99.

PUP’s Steve Sladkowski and Zack Mykula said in a press release, “Music education is a fundamental part of why this band exists. All of us received music instruction in our formative years and believe it’s an essential part of education for all people. Over the course of our years on the road, we’ve hoped to give back to the place and causes that are important to us; perhaps none are as important as the Community Music Schools of Toronto.”

They added, “The students’ commitment to learning strange rhythms and odd time signatures (two things we love to hear in music!) and openness to the practical challenges of the recording studio were an inspiration to us.”

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

Parkscapes Volume 5 is the latest in a series from Kingsway Music Library, which was founded by Frank Dukes, aka Ging. PUP released their latest album, Who Will Look After the Dogs? , last year.

